{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1786969131,"nonce":"OoZE9VWKiFGbnRiWxK9NmLCdFxw=","title":"Every empty state is the same fūrin, so `expired` — the one state that means transience — looks identical to a filter that matched nothing","message":"**The demonstration.** Every empty state in the product is the same 32 px fūrin over a sentence — `web/src/components/ui/states.tsx:34-52`, whose own comment at `:38-39` calls the glyph \"the only decorative art in the app\". Filter the alert list to nothing and you get it; open an alert whose delivery panel is empty and you get it; land on a tenant with no sources and you get it. `expired` gets it too, which is the problem: `expired` is the one state in the system whose meaning is *transience* — §M.1 is explicit that it reads \"oto stopped hearing about this\", never \"resolved\" — and on screen it is indistinguishable from a filter that matched nothing.\n\n**Why it matters.** These are the states an ops tool spends most of its life in; `states.tsx:1-15` says so and holds them to a standard of honesty about *why* a panel is empty. The copy already does that work. Nothing visual supports it, so two facts that the file goes out of its way to keep distinct — \"nothing matched\" versus \"the source went quiet and oto refuses to call that resolved\" — arrive looking identical.\n\nTwo motifs, one each, chosen because their traditional meaning already matches the state rather than because they are decorative. **Kumo** — cloud, stillness — on a quiet state: nothing is wrong, and that is the point. **Sakura** — mono no aware, transience — on `expired`, and nowhere else, because a petal that appears on every empty panel stops meaning transience within a day. Corner-anchored, `--oto-wash`, static, never touching the text.\n\nTwo constraints that are not negotiable and are easy to lose. **One motif per state, never both**: the moment a panel carries clouds *and* petals the distinction they exist to draw is gone. And **U1**: the motif is a second channel beside the sentence, never a substitute for it, so the copy must still say the whole fact with the ink removed. The obvious next thought — drifting clouds, falling petals — is forbidden by U9 (ADR 0028): a purely decorative one-shot fires at most once per document and the fūrin's 180 ms greeting already owns that budget.\n\n**The wash must not go on the shared `EmptyState`.** It has 18 call sites and six of them are sub-panels on a single alert-detail page — `DeliveryPanel.tsx:92`, `EnrichmentPanel.tsx:63`, `OccurrencePanel.tsx:83`, `Timeline.tsx:85`, `RuleDrift.tsx:467`, `SnoozePanel.tsx:55` — so a wash on the shared component renders six of them on one quiet alert. This wants a distinct full-page component, or a prop gated to the full-page call sites only.\n\n**Where.** `web/src/components/ui/states.tsx:34-52` (`EmptyState`, and the six-at-once trap), `:38-40` (the fūrin and the \"only decorative art\" comment this amends); full-page call sites `web/src/routes/alerts.tsx:487`, `:505`, `:542`, `:557`, `web/src/routes/groups.tsx:229`, `web/src/features/notifications/PoliciesSection.tsx:310`; the six sub-panel call sites listed above, which must **not** receive it; `web/src/components/ui/Chime.tsx:98-110` (`BOX` and the per-size `STROKE`, and the ⛔ block explaining why one shared stroke width is wrong — a wash-scale bell would need a third entry, and `Chime.test.tsx` pins them); `docs/design/SPEC.md:4926` (U1), `:4934` (U9); `docs/adr/0028-non-urgency-motion-one-shots-and-activity-loops.md`.\n\n**Scope.** small — two SVG assets and one new component, gated to six call sites. It depends on the primitive.\n\n**Done when.** A full-page empty state can carry an ambient motif; quiet states carry kumo and `expired` carries sakura; no panel carries both. The shared `EmptyState` is untouched, so one quiet alert still renders six plain sub-panels rather than six washes. Every motif is `aria-hidden`, static, and clear of the text, and each empty state still reads correctly with the ink removed.","files":null}]}